00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:48.480
Their span is some subspace of
what?

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:52.860
Their span, which is this sort
of plain looking thing I've

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:57.360
drawn, it's a subspace of what?

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.460
Subspace of R what?

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:01.160
Rn,

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.540
good, because the vectors all
live in Rn.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:06.380
There are just d of them.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:09.240
Their span is some subspace of
Rn.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.620
The question I want to try and
answer is,

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.540
you,

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:16.940
let's suppose it's not in the
subspace, necessarily.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.140
It's in Rn, but it's not
necessarily in the span of the

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:19.860
v's.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:20.860
The question is,

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:26.200
how do I find the vector in the
subspace that is closest to you,

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.300
okay? Why do I want to answer
